#
# Declarative structural assertions for the pipeline slice (Tier-B
# closeout). The repo-level narrow-waist/transpile tests check pipeline BEHAVIOR
# (KEEP); these cells pin the slice's asserted-TBox spine and the integrity of
# its dogfooded build-pipeline ABox fresh (MAXIMAL coverage, dogfooding). Each
# runs as a SPARQL ASK over the module graph (gmeow:scopeModule).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/pipeline/tests/> .

# --- 1. Pipeline / PipelineStage / StageCapability spine (MUST hold) ---------
ex:saPipelineKinds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:Pipeline        a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Plan , gmeow:SocialObject .
    gmeow:PipelineStage   a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:ActionSchema , gmeow:SocialObject .
    gmeow:StageCapability a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:Pipeline MUST be a logic:Plan (the build re-seated under the canonical process model) AND a gmeow:SocialObject (logic:Plan grounds its social-object sort in prose, not by a subclass edge, so the asserted edge is independent and load-bearing). gmeow:PipelineStage is a logic:ActionSchema SocialObject — a typed unit of work whose resource/capability declarations the scheduler reads in place of a kind enum. gmeow:StageCapability is a QualityValue vocabulary of declared stage capabilities (sink, source-origin)." .

# --- 5. Pipeline is a DAG-workflow projection of logic:Plan (MUST hold) -------
ex:saPipelineDagProfileSeating a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:dataflowConsumes rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:dataflowConsumes .
    gmeow:dataflowProduces rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:dataflowProduces .
    gmeow:pipeline-build
        logic:planGoal           gmeow:goalShippableBundle ;
        logic:planSuccessMode    logic:StrongPlanSuccess ;
        logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract .
    gmeow:goalShippableBundle a gmeow:Goal .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The pipeline MUST be a projection of the one canonical process model, not a parallel one: gmeow:dataflowConsumes/dataflowProduces specialize the canonical logic:dataflowConsumes/dataflowProduces, and the build plan gmeow:pipeline-build carries its logic:planGoal (the shippable bundle), logic:planSuccessMode (StrongPlanSuccess — the deterministic build reaches the goal every run, satisfying logic:PlanShape), and runs logic:executedUnderContract the DAG-workflow profile under which its acyclic dataflow closure is certified." .

# --- 2. Dataflow and stage property shapes (MUST hold) -----------------------
ex:saPipelinePropertyShapes a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:hasStage         a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:Pipeline ;      rdfs:range gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:dataflowConsumes a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ; rdfs:range gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:dataflowProduces a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ; rdfs:range gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:hasCapability    a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ; rdfs:range gmeow:StageCapability .
    gmeow:requiresResource a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ; rdfs:range gmeow:Resource .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The pipeline edges MUST hold their shapes: gmeow:hasStage (Pipeline→Stage), the gmeow:dataflowConsumes/dataflowProduces dataflow (Stage→Stage), gmeow:hasCapability (Stage→StageCapability), and gmeow:requiresResource (Stage→Resource)." .

# --- 3. The seeded StageCapability value vocabulary (MUST hold) --------------
ex:saStageCapabilitySeeds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:sinkCapability a gmeow:StageCapability .
    gmeow:sourceOrigin   a gmeow:StageCapability .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The StageCapability value vocabulary MUST seed the two declared stage capabilities the executor reads in place of a kind enum: gmeow:sinkCapability (the single serialization exit / narrow waist) and gmeow:sourceOrigin (the authored-source loader, whose products are provenance-origin Source)." .

# --- 4. The source loader and the sink carry their capabilities (MUST hold) ----
ex:saStageCapabilityHolders a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:stage-source-load gmeow:hasCapability gmeow:sourceOrigin .
    gmeow:stage-gts-sink     gmeow:hasCapability gmeow:sinkCapability .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Integrity of the dogfooded build pipeline: the authored-source loader MUST hold gmeow:sourceOrigin (so its emitted quads' provenance origin is Source) and the single serialization exit MUST hold gmeow:sinkCapability (the narrow waist the loader requires exactly one stage to hold) — the capability declarations the executor reads instead of a kind enum." .

# --- 4b. NO OTHER stage carries either capability (MUST NOT hold) --------------
# The positive assertion above only proves the designated holders carry their
# capability; this pins EXCLUSIVITY. A spurious second gmeow:sinkCapability holder
# would break the narrow waist, and a spurious gmeow:sourceOrigin holder would mark a
# non-source stage's products provenance-origin Source — both corruptions the loader
# rejects (sink) or never intends (source). Neither must exist in the build module.
ex:saStageCapabilityHolderExclusivity a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    { ?s gmeow:hasCapability gmeow:sinkCapability . FILTER(?s != gmeow:stage-gts-sink) }
    UNION
    { ?s gmeow:hasCapability gmeow:sourceOrigin . FILTER(?s != gmeow:stage-source-load) }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Exclusivity of the dogfooded build pipeline's capability holders: no stage other than gmeow:stage-gts-sink may hold gmeow:sinkCapability (the single serialization exit) and no stage other than gmeow:stage-source-load may hold gmeow:sourceOrigin (the sole authored-source loader). A spurious holder of either would corrupt the narrow-waist or provenance-origin contract the executor relies on." .

# --- 6. Stage-contribution + fanout vocabulary is declared (MUST hold) --------
# The run-verified contribution predicates (gmeow:attachesGraph / gmeow:attachesBlobRep,
# PIPELINE_SPINE §3.3) and the promoted fanout path↔representative map
# (gmeow:fanoutExtracts over gmeow:FanoutExtraction) MUST carry their TBox spine so the
# loader's Rust/RDF attach agreement and the superset gate's data-driven reconstruction
# read a declared vocabulary, not undeclared symbols.
ex:saAttachAndFanoutVocab a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    gmeow:attachesGraph    a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:attachesBlobRep  a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:FanoutExtraction a owl:Class .
    gmeow:fanoutExtracts   a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:Pipeline ; rdfs:range gmeow:FanoutExtraction .
    gmeow:extractsPath     a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:FanoutExtraction .
    gmeow:extractsForm     a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:FanoutExtraction .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The stage-contribution predicates (gmeow:attachesGraph → each named graph a stage attaches to the carrier as its delta; gmeow:attachesBlobRep → each blob-representation lane) and the promoted fanout map (gmeow:fanoutExtracts gathering gmeow:FanoutExtraction rows of gmeow:extractsPath / gmeow:extractsForm) MUST be TBox-declared with their domains: the scheduler HARD-fails on attach-declaration drift and the superset gate reconstructs generated/ paths from these rows, so both must read a declared vocabulary." .

# --- 7. Every declared stage attach is a carrier graph/blob, not a stage (MUST NOT) ---
# gmeow:attachesGraph names named-graph IRIs (graph/...), never a gmeow:PipelineStage.
# A stage mistakenly named as an attached graph would corrupt the run-time delta compare.
ex:saAttachesGraphIsNotAStage a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK { ?stage gmeow:attachesGraph ?g . ?g a gmeow:PipelineStage . }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:attachesGraph relates a stage to a carrier NAMED-GRAPH IRI (its attach delta), never to another pipeline stage; a stage object here would mean the run-time delta compare is checking against a stage, not a graph." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Runtime-DAG vocabulary (issue #1674) — TBox spine + closed value seeds.       #
# =========================================================================== #

# --- 8. The runtime-DAG class spine (MUST hold) ------------------------------
ex:saRuntimeDagKinds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:FlowReason      a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:StageDisposition a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:StageObligation a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:StageStability  a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:StageExecution  a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Event .
    gmeow:PipelineRun     a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Event .
    gmeow:StageBudget     a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:SocialObject .
    gmeow:StageReceipt    a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:SocialObject .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The general runtime-DAG vocabulary (issue #1674) MUST carry its TBox spine: gmeow:FlowReason / gmeow:StageDisposition / gmeow:StageObligation / gmeow:StageStability are QualityValue vocabularies (closed value classes); gmeow:StageExecution and gmeow:PipelineRun are perdurant occurrences (logic:Event) — one run of a stage and one run of a whole DAG; gmeow:StageBudget and gmeow:StageReceipt are reified SocialObject records (a per-stage budget and a content-addressed receipt)." .

# --- 9. The closed FlowReason value vocabulary (MUST hold) --------------------
ex:saFlowReasonSeeds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:flowReasonDataflow  a gmeow:FlowReason .
    gmeow:flowReasonAuthority a gmeow:FlowReason .
    gmeow:flowReasonCost      a gmeow:FlowReason .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The FlowReason value vocabulary MUST seed exactly the three declared edge reasons: gmeow:flowReasonDataflow (bytes flow), gmeow:flowReasonAuthority (a first-class ordering a pure-dataflow reasoner must not drop), and gmeow:flowReasonCost (resource-serialization). The set is closed at three." .

# --- 9b. No FlowReason individual outside the closed three (MUST NOT) ----------
ex:saFlowReasonClosed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    ?r a gmeow:FlowReason .
    FILTER(?r NOT IN (gmeow:flowReasonDataflow, gmeow:flowReasonAuthority, gmeow:flowReasonCost))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The FlowReason set is CLOSED: a fourth reason individual would let an edge be typed with an unrecognized reason the admission constraint does not account for, silently weakening the dataflow/authority/cost distinction." .

# --- 10. The closed StageDisposition value vocabulary (MUST hold) -------------
ex:saDispositionSeeds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:dispositionCompleted        a gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:dispositionTypedAbsence     a gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:dispositionRejectedCandidate a gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:dispositionRetryable        a gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:dispositionFatalToCandidate a gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:dispositionTimedOut         a gmeow:StageDisposition .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The StageDisposition vocabulary MUST seed exactly the six declared per-execution outcomes: completed, typed-absence (an explicit typed nothing — a valid answer), rejected-candidate, retryable, fatal-to-candidate, and timed-out. Typed dispositions replace an untyped success/failure boolean; the set is closed at six." .

# --- 11. The closed StageObligation and StageStability seeds (MUST hold) ------
ex:saObligationStabilitySeeds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:obligationMandatory     a gmeow:StageObligation .
    gmeow:obligationDegradable    a gmeow:StageObligation .
    gmeow:stabilityStablePrefix   a gmeow:StageStability .
    gmeow:stabilityPerTurnVariance a gmeow:StageStability .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The stage-level declarations MUST seed their closed sets: gmeow:StageObligation over {mandatory, degradable} ('this stage's absence invalidates the run' is a declared property), and gmeow:StageStability over {stablePrefix (byte-identical across turns — enables prefix-cache ordering), perTurnVariance}." .

# --- 12. The runtime-DAG property shapes (MUST hold) -------------------------
ex:saRuntimeDagProperties a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:flowReason       a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:BuildDataFlow ;  rdfs:range gmeow:FlowReason .
    gmeow:stageDisposition a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:StageExecution ; rdfs:range gmeow:StageDisposition .
    gmeow:stageObligation  a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ;  rdfs:range gmeow:StageObligation .
    gmeow:stageStability   a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ;  rdfs:range gmeow:StageStability .
    gmeow:hasStageBudget   a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineStage ;  rdfs:range gmeow:StageBudget .
    gmeow:budgetDeadline   a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageBudget ;    rdfs:range xsd:duration .
    gmeow:budgetMaxSteps   a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageBudget ;    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
    gmeow:budgetMaxAnswers a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageBudget ;    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
    gmeow:budgetMaxInputBytes  a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageBudget ; rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
    gmeow:budgetMaxMemoryBytes a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageBudget ; rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
    gmeow:hasStageReceipt  a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:PipelineRun ;    rdfs:range gmeow:StageReceipt .
    gmeow:receiptOfStage   a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:domain gmeow:StageReceipt ;   rdfs:range gmeow:PipelineStage .
    gmeow:receiptDigest    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:StageReceipt ;   rdfs:range xsd:string .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The runtime-DAG properties MUST hold their shapes: the required edge reason (gmeow:flowReason: BuildDataFlow→FlowReason), the per-execution disposition (StageExecution→StageDisposition), the stage-level obligation and stability (PipelineStage→StageObligation/StageStability), the per-stage budget (gmeow:hasStageBudget plus the five typed-literal ceilings on gmeow:StageBudget), and the run receipts (gmeow:hasStageReceipt: PipelineRun→StageReceipt, gmeow:receiptOfStage: StageReceipt→PipelineStage, gmeow:receiptDigest: StageReceipt→xsd:string)." .

# --- 13. Every gmeow:BuildDataFlow carries a flow reason (MUST NOT be absent) --
# gmeow:flowReason is REQUIRED on gmeow:BuildDataFlow, so no reified edge (including
# the build DAG's own five) may lack it; the five build edges are byte dependencies.
ex:saEveryBuildEdgeHasFlowReason a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK { ?e a gmeow:BuildDataFlow . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?e gmeow:flowReason ?r } }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:flowReason is REQUIRED on gmeow:BuildDataFlow (min-qualified-cardinality 1): an edge with no reason is indistinguishable from a droppable dataflow dependency, so the build DAG's own five reified edges each declare gmeow:flowReasonDataflow and no edge may be reason-less." .

# --- 14. The runtime-DAG admission constraint is authored in logic: (MUST) ----
# A logic:Constraint carrying an integrity formula and a message, NOT a hand-authored
# SHACL shape (projection-purity: validation is authored in logic: only).
ex:saAdmissionConstraint a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:RuntimeDagAdmissionConstraint a logic:Constraint ;
        logic:integrity ?f ;
        logic:message ?m ;
        logic:severity "Violation" .
    ?f logic:and gmeow:radDataflowForall , gmeow:radAuthorityForall .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The admission law MUST be authored as a logic:Constraint + logic:Formula (never a hand-authored SHACL shape): its logic:integrity conjoins the dataflow-producer-existence and authority-edge-retention first-order arms, its logic:message states all four expectations (acyclicity, connectivity, dataflow satisfaction, authority satisfaction), and the transitive-closure arms are disclosed via the honest gmeow:runtimeDagAdmissionBoundary rather than faked." .
